  "notes": "Wikimedia Commons upload of 2018-08-06 by QYYZ, vectorised from a Hasselblad press-release PDF (cdn.hasselblad.com). Source had one <g transform=\"matrix(1,0,0,1,-197,-72)\">; translate baked into coordinates. Removed a stray unstyled 2-point zero-area line (M198.425,82.431L198.852,81.085). Each L was two abutting pieces (stroke + base bar, 0.003-unit seam); merged into one polygon per L to avoid antialias seams. Ten paths, one per letter, each nonzero: the A and B counters are cut by opposite path direction, and some letters retrace edges, so DO NOT merge them into a single path or switch them to evenodd. Original grey fill rgb(55,53,53) dropped (app colours it). The crossbars of H, A, E and B deliberately extend left of the letters; that is the real logo design. Very wide (~12.8:1) horizontal wordmark. Hasselblad makes medium-format camera bodies and XCD lenses; kind set to camera per request."
